{"name":"Celine","hex":"#826167","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Celine","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A female given name from Latin."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Celine"}],"entries":[{"title":"Celine (concert residency)","blocks":[{"text":"Celine was the second concert residency by Canadian singer Celine Dion. It was staged at The Colosseum at Caesars Palace on the Las Vegas Strip in Paradise, Nevada, beginning 15 March 2011, with an estimated seventy performances per year. The residency ranked 26th in Pollstar's \"Top 50 Worldwide Tour (Mid-Year)\", earning over $20 million. Seen by more than 200,000 people, it became the number one show in 2011 for North America. It made Dion the top earner in Las Vegas, with $500,000 per show, and led to her being described as the \"most profitable music act in Las Vegas\" since Elvis Presley."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/fb/CDion_2015residencyshowposter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Celine_(concert_residency)","wikidata":"Q666450"},{"title":"Celine (brand)","blocks":[{"text":"Celine is a French luxury fashion house founded in 1945 by fashion designer Céline Vipiana. The headquarters are located at 16 rue Vivienne in the 2nd arrondissement of Paris at the Hôtel Colbert de Torcy, which has French Historic Monument classification."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/20230417_Celine_store_at_David_Plaza.jpg/330px-20230417_Celine_store_at_David_Plaza.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Celine_(brand)","wikidata":"Q948531"},{"title":"Céline","blocks":[{"text":"Céline, sometimes spelled Celine, is a French female first name version of Latin origin, coming from Caelīna, the feminine form of the Roman cognomen Caelīnus, meaning \"heavenly\". Its equivalent in Spanish, Italian, and Portuguese is Celina. Céline was frequently chosen as a first name in honour of two Gallo-Roman saints closely associated with the beginnings of the French nation:"}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/C%C3%A9line","wikidata":"Q18147692"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/6/68/Celine_Dion_My_Heart_Will_Go_On_Las_Vegas_2011.jpg/250px-Celine_Dion_My_Heart_Will_Go_On_Las_Vegas_2011.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/68/Celine_Dion_My_Heart_Will_Go_On_Las_Vegas_2011.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/6/68/Celine_Dion_My_Heart_Will_Go_On_Las_Vegas_2011.jpg/250px-Celine_Dion_My_Heart_Will_Go_On_Las_Vegas_2011.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Dion performing \"My Heart Will Go On\" on opening night (15 March 2011).","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACeline_Dion_My_Heart_Will_Go_On_Las_Vegas_2011.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Madrid_-_Celine_%28Calle_de_Jos%C3%A9_Ortega_y_Gasset_16%29.jpg/500px-Madrid_-_Celine_%28Calle_de_Jos%C3%A9_Ortega_y_Gasset_16%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Madrid_-_Celine_%28Calle_de_Jos%C3%A9_Ortega_y_Gasset_16%29.jpg/1280px-Madrid_-_Celine_%28Calle_de_Jos%C3%A9_Ortega_y_Gasset_16%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Madrid_-_Celine_%28Calle_de_Jos%C3%A9_Ortega_y_Gasset_16%29.jpg/500px-Madrid_-_Celine_%28Calle_de_Jos%C3%A9_Ortega_y_Gasset_16%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMadri